<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" class="aligned-bullets" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 14px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 21px; padding-bottom: 40px; width: 100%;"> <p style="margin: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 22px; line-height: 33px;"><strong>Student Financial Software Webinar&nbsp;</strong></span></p> <p style="margin: 0px;">‌<br /></p> <p style="margin: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 21px;"><strong>21st January 2026 </strong></span></p> <p style="margin: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 21px;"><strong>10:00 AM - 11:00 AM</strong></span></p> <p style="margin: 0px;">‌<br /></p> <p style="margin: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 21px;">Join our SFS webinar via Zoom, hosted by Mark Gilbert, Senior Technical Consultant, Flywire who recently joined the team from Anglia Ruskin University. <br />Mark will be providing an overview of SFS, covering the latest insights and product developments, including a thorough live demonstration. This will be an interactive webinar where you'll have the opportunity to engage and ask questions throughout.<br /><br /> </span></p> <p style="margin: 0px;"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 21px;">While this webinar is primarily aimed at Unit4 clients, we will also share an update on our progress with integrating SFS with other systems.</span></p> </td> 
